From: Claude (Anthropic AI) <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Fri, 5 Sep 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] winewayland: Don't require presentation ownership to stack a
 covering client above the carrier.

wayland_client_surface_should_stack_above_parent() refuses the
stack-above-carrier path unless the client surface is the window's
presentation owner. For Vulkan clients that election never runs on this
path: wayland_client_surface_update_owner() is only reached from the
client_surface destroy/detach/update callbacks and set_client_surface(),
and the "presentation owner X -> Y" trace never fires for a D3D12 title.

The check therefore rejects every Vulkan game and forces transparent
punch-through compositing. On compositors that skip the parent/child blend
for fullscreen windows the client content never reaches the screen, which
reproduces the fullscreen black screen this series was meant to fix
(Cyberpunk 2077 and The Witcher 3 on Hyprland, native Wayland, both SDR and
HDR; XWayland and windowed mode unaffected).

Instrumenting the predicate showed presentation_owner as the sole rejecting
condition, 5639 times in a single run, with geometry already perfect
(window and client rects both 3840x2160).

Drop it as a requirement and keep it only as trace output. The remaining
conditions - single toplevel client, no GDI content over the producer, no
alpha, not layered/shaped/minimised, window rect equal to client rect, no
dmabuf stack below - already constrain this to the intended case. The
predicate now also reports which condition rejected it, so future reports
name a specific check instead of guesswork.
---
 dlls/winewayland.drv/wayland_surface.c | 40 ++++++++++++++++++++------
 1 file changed, 31 insertions(+), 9 deletions(-)

--- a/dlls/winewayland.drv/wayland_surface.c
+++ b/dlls/winewayland.drv/wayland_surface.c
@@ -2477,19 +2477,36 @@
         struct wayland_surface *surface, struct wayland_client_surface *client,
         HWND hwnd, HWND toplevel, BOOL content_over_producer)
 {
-    if (!ReadAcquire(&client->client.presentation_owner)) return FALSE;
+    BOOL owner = !!ReadAcquire(&client->client.presentation_owner);
+    const char *reject = NULL;
+
     /* A single opaque client surface covering the whole toplevel can sit above
-     * an opaque parent carrier without using transparent punch-through. */
-    if (hwnd != toplevel) return FALSE;
-    if (content_over_producer || ReadAcquire(&client->has_alpha)) return FALSE;
-    if (surface->window.exstyle & WS_EX_LAYERED) return FALSE;
-    if (!wayland_surface_is_toplevel(surface) || surface->window.minimized) return FALSE;
+     * an opaque parent carrier without using transparent punch-through.
+     *
+     * presentation_owner is deliberately NOT required here: for Vulkan clients
+     * the ownership election never runs on this path, so requiring it kept
+     * every D3D12/Vulkan game on punch-through and black-screened them on
+     * compositors that skip the parent/child blend in fullscreen. The
+     * remaining checks already constrain this to a single, opaque,
+     * fully-covering toplevel client. */
+    if (hwnd != toplevel) reject = "hwnd != toplevel";
+    else if (content_over_producer) reject = "content_over_producer";
+    else if (ReadAcquire(&client->has_alpha)) reject = "has_alpha";
+    else if (surface->window.exstyle & WS_EX_LAYERED) reject = "WS_EX_LAYERED";
+    else if (!wayland_surface_is_toplevel(surface)) reject = "not toplevel";
+    else if (surface->window.minimized) reject = "minimized";
     /* The outer Win32 rect may retain stale frame extents across a fullscreen
      * transition; classify coverage against the Wayland presentation rect. */
-    if (!EqualRect(&surface->window.rect, &surface->window.client_rect)) return FALSE;
-    if (surface->shaped) return FALSE;
-    if (wayland_surface_dmabuf_stack_bottom(surface)) return FALSE;
-    return TRUE;
+    else if (!EqualRect(&surface->window.rect, &surface->window.client_rect)) reject = "rect != client_rect";
+    else if (surface->shaped) reject = "shaped";
+    else if (wayland_surface_dmabuf_stack_bottom(surface)) reject = "dmabuf_stack_bottom";
+
+    TRACE("hwnd=%p stack_above=%d reject=%s owner=%d window=%s client=%s\n",
+          hwnd, !reject, reject ? reject : "(none)", owner,
+          wine_dbgstr_rect(&surface->window.rect),
+          wine_dbgstr_rect(&surface->window.client_rect));
+
+    return !reject;
 }
 
 static void wayland_client_surface_stack(struct wayland_surface *surface,
